    description: "Dharug National Park covers 148.5 sq km on the Hawkesbury River and was established in 1967. It holds the Old Great North Road, built by up to 720 convicts between 1826 and 1836, and its Devine's Hill and Finch's Line sections were inscribed as part of the Australian Convict Sites World Heritage listing in 2010. Wisemans Ferry, where a free cable ferry has crossed the river since 1829, is the usual gateway. The park can be walked, cycled, paddled or camped.",
