    description: "Dubbo is a city of 43,516 people (2021) in the Orana region, about 392 km north-west of Sydney. Taronga Western Plains Zoo, an open-range zoo with elephants, giraffes and a breeding program for rare black rhinos, is the district's biggest tourist draw. In town, Old Dubbo Gaol, an official gaol from 1859 to 1966, is now a museum, and the Royal Flying Doctor Service has a hands-on visitor experience at the airport. Wellington Caves, with guided tours of Cathedral Cave and Gaden Cave, is the usual day trip.",
