    description: "The Hunter Valley is New South Wales's wine region, one of the first planted in Australia, in the early 19th century, and now home to over 150 wineries. Around Pokolbin the vineyards and small villages have no single centre, with Cessnock the service town and Maitland, Morpeth and Wollombi holding heritage buildings. Semillon and Shiraz are the best-known wines, and Watagans National Park's rainforest lies an hour from Newcastle. The Hunter has been overtaken by the Riverina as NSW's biggest producer and makes about 3% of Australia's wine.",
